   185	SHAPE-KILL §3.3 names the exact missing ingredient for every `g`-cabled row: *"the
   186	missing ingredient is the inner braid `iota`, numerically pinned by (1.1) to
   187	`e(iota) = (d-1) + 2 delta_aff - n(d-g)` but not otherwise constrained without a
   188	`delta_aff` census."* At `g = 2` the tube braid group is `B_2 = <sigma> = Z`, which
   189	is **abelian**, so the exponent sum is a *complete* invariant of each tube factor,
   190	and (1.1) is not a partial pin but the whole of `iota` up to the distribution among
   191	tubes — which, as the proof shows, drops out. This lane has the `delta_aff` census
   192	(§1). So the ingredient is available here and nowhere else in the campaign.
   193	
   194	> **THEOREM TUBE-2 (PROVED-HERE, UNREVIEWED).** *Let `D` be a residual branch curve
   195	> of type `(d,n)` with `g = gcd(d,n) = 2`, `d' = d/2`, `n' = n/2`, `gcd(d',n') = 1`,
   196	> `d' > n'`, and suppose `phi : pi_1(C^2 - D) ->> S_4` sends every meridian to a
   197	> transposition and has non-constant block products. Put `E := e(iota)` as in (1.1)
   198	> and `h := Pi^{d'-1} Pi_{d'}^{-(d'-1)}`. Then the block subtuple `T_1 = (u,v)` of the
   199	> `rho_inf`-fixed tuple satisfies*
   200	>
   201	> ```text
   202	> (4.1)     T_1  =  c_h ( sigma^E . T_1 ) ,        c_h(x) := h x h^{-1} entrywise.
   203	> ```
   204	>
   205	> *In family 3 (`(d',n') = (4,3)`) one has `h = 1` and hence `T_1 = sigma^E . T_1`;
   206	> the stabiliser of a non-constant `T_1` in `B_2 = Z` is exactly `3Z`, so*
   207	>
   208	> ```text
   209	> (4.2)     3 | e(iota)   is NECESSARY  for  phi  to exist on a family-3, g=2 row.
   210	> ```
   211	
   212	*Proof.* Write `T = (T_1,...,T_{d'})` in blocks, `S := iota . T`. Since the left
   213	Hurwitz action satisfies `(beta gamma) . T = beta . (gamma . T)`, `rho_inf . T = T`
   214	reads `C_2(delta_{d'}^{n'}) . S = T`. The block-level action of `delta_{d'}` is
   215	`(u_1,...,u_{d'}) -> (Pi u_{d'} Pi^{-1}, u_1, ..., u_{d'-1})` (promoted, §3.3 of the
   216	decision report), and its blackboard cable acts on block tuples by
   217	`(B_1,...,B_{d'}) -> (P B_{d'} P^{-1}, B_1,...,B_{d'-1})` with `P = Pi_1 ... Pi_{d'-1}
   218	= Pi Pi_{d'}^{-1}` (entrywise conjugation; the promoted Lemma 3.3 computation
   219	`C_g(sigma_i).(A,B) = (Pi_A B Pi_A^{-1}, A)` composed along `delta_{d'} = sigma_1...sigma_{d'-1}`).
   220	Note the conjugator is `Pi Pi_{d'}^{-1}` and **not** `Pi`: for a single entry the two
   221	agree, for a block they do not. Internal check on the assignment: applying block
   222	products to the four relations gives `Pi(T_1) = Pi B Pi^{-1} = A`,
   223	`Pi(T_2) = Pi C Pi^{-1} = B`, `Pi(T_3) = Pi A Pi^{-1} = C`, `Pi(T_4) = A` — all four
   224	match `(Pi_1,...,Pi_4) = (A,B,C,A)`, which a mis-assigned conjugator would break.
   225	
   226	At `(d',n') = (4,3)`, three applications give
   227	`C_2(delta_4^3) . S = (c_{Pi B^{-1}}(S_2), c_{Pi C^{-1}}(S_3), c_{Pi A^{-1}}(S_4), S_1) = T`.
   228	Since `iota` acts blockwise and preserves block products, `S_i = sigma^{a_i} . T_i`
   229	with `sum a_i = E`. Conjugation commutes with the Hurwitz action (the action is by
   230	words in the entries), and `B_2` is abelian, so composing the four relations around
   231	the cycle `T_1 <- T_2 <- T_3 <- T_4 <- T_1` gives
   232	`T_1 = c_h(sigma^{a_1+a_2+a_3+a_4} . T_1)` with
   233	`h = (Pi B^{-1})(Pi C^{-1})(Pi A^{-1})`. Using `Pi^{-1} B Pi = C`, `Pi^{-1} C Pi = A`
   234	(i.e. (4.1) of SHAPE-KILL) this collapses to `h = Pi^3 A^{-3}`, and `ord(Pi) = 3`
   235	(SK-5) with `ord(A) = 3` give `h = 1`. **Only the sum `E` survives; the distribution
   236	of `iota` among the four tubes is irrelevant.**
