   238	Finally, the `B_2`-orbit. With `A = uv = (abc)`, `sigma . (u,v) = (uvu^{-1}, u)` sends
   239	`((ac),(ab)) -> ((bc),(ca)) -> ((ab),(bc)) -> ((ac),(ab))`: `sigma` permutes the three
   240	factorisations in a `3`-cycle. Hence the stabiliser of any one of them is `3Z`, and
   241	`sigma^E . T_1 = T_1` iff `3 | E`. (Equivalently: `sigma^2 = c_A`, so `sigma^6` acts
   242	trivially, `sigma^{2k}` fixes iff `3 | k` — `Z(S_3) = 1` — and `sigma^{2k+1}` fixes iff
   243	`k = 1 mod 3`; the two branches merge to `3 | E`.) `[]`
