./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:9:The algebraic recursion and generated Singular contracts are source-complete, but the AWS custody path is not safe for a pilot. The late authority accepts an allowlisted copied candidate without binding it to the independent classifier output, and it reads that live candidate only after freezing the terminal archive. A bounded no-verdict candidate can therefore be replaced by the dead or survivor string and promoted; the public marker can also disagree with the reviewed archive. Dynamic stage records are not bound to the current job identity/nonce or regenerated by the classifier, and the supervisor has no fail-safe containment on supervisor `SIGKILL`/death. These are promotion and custody defects, not residual mathematical uncertainty.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:107:The implementation checks precisely these conditions. Reduced intermediate powers remain congruent to the corresponding pure powers modulo `I`, so a final zero normal form is a valid membership witness. The proper branch searches exponents 0..64 separately per basis generator. If any search exhausts, the script prints the reverse-exhaustion marker and quits before `SATURATION_CERTIFICATE_COMPLETE`; the driver emits only the bounded no-verdict. The 257-step pure-delta search is entered only on the empty-open branch. The strict-overideal adapter fixture correctly shows why inclusion plus stability alone is insufficient.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:113:Rank scripts enumerate every support-matchable minor and use Hall matching to certify all omitted structural zeros. Every skipped size requires the all-zero marker; the first nonzero witness fixes the rank. The inherited bound is nonincreasing.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:131:The allowlist contains exactly four strings: closed-successor finite-cover dead, chart-local ring-level survivor pending nilpotence/radical, bounded open remainder, and reverse-search exhaustion. The first two make no whole-stratum, radical, geometric, or JC2 claim; the latter two make no mathematical conclusion. Worker source never writes `TERMINAL.marker`; the supervisor is the only in-packet public-marker authority, using mutually exclusive normal and emergency paths.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:141:This admits both pre-freeze copied-field substitution and post-freeze disagreement between archive and marker. It also leaves `FINALIZATION_LATCHES.txt`, the decision transcript, and the promoted marker outside the reviewed archive. Required repair: bank one content-addressed decision record binding job tag/nonce, source-archive hash, lease/worker identity, production and classifier summary/verdict hashes, complete artifact-manifest hash, and candidate; have the late authority verify all equalities against the freshly extracted archive; bind the public marker to the archive/decision digest; and eliminate the live post-archive candidate reread.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:147:The accepted synthetic fixtures prove the gap: arbitrary one-line fixture scripts and no identity files pass the real dead/survivor classifier when paired with fabricated marker transcripts and matching self-hashes. Required repair: make the classifier regenerate and byte-compare every dynamic script and required artifact set, verify current-job identity JSON and its hash from each result, verify runner/child starttime/uid/PGID/SID/job tag/cgroup/cap/argv/Singular digest, and reject copied or missing identities. The bounded no-verdict chain must likewise be compared to the driver's exact remainder literals, hashes, bound, stage sequence, and reason.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:151:TERM/INT/HUP/normal EXIT run cleanup, but `SIGKILL` or abrupt supervisor death cannot run traps. The transient systemd scope has `MemoryMax`/`TasksMax` but no independent runtime deadline or supervisor-death kill binding. The PGID fallback also has no `PR_SET_PDEATHSIG`, parent-starttime watchdog, or external lease monitor. A worker/CAS tree can therefore continue after supervisor death, with neither the 21,600-second whole-job enforcement nor a terminal. It should not produce a mathematical marker, but it violates bounded custody and cleanup.
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:161:| Nonce and lease | Partial/fail: atomic fresh `JOB_ROOT` is a useful namespace lease and IMDS tag/source hash are checked, but the suffix may be empty, no nonce schema is enforced, and stage/candidate/marker records are not nonce-bound. |
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:162:| Stale namespace | Intended launcher rejects an existing root/archive/marker. Direct supervisor invocation has no independent lease acquisition, so the guarantee depends on always entering through the exact launcher. |
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:163:| Duplicate terminal writers | Worker writes only a candidate. One supervisor process owns the public marker; normal and trapped emergency paths are mutually exclusive in ordinary control flow. Publication uses ordinary `mv`, not no-replace installation, and is not bound to the archive, so same-UID/rerun races remain. |
./xmodel/triple02-node1-closed-successor-resume-r1-hostile-review-sol56-20260829.md:170:| Success after a listed Boolean fault | Pure `decide_terminal` mutations downgrade to custody no-verdict. Copied-candidate/job-binding faults are not gate inputs and can still produce a mathematical marker; therefore the overall attack fails. |
